# Next.js BFF + UI

## Data access

- Browser: `apiFetch` / domain helpers in `src/lib/api/` → `/api/proxy`.
- Auth UI: `authFetch('/api/auth/...')` — not `/api/proxy/auth/...`.
- Server→Rust: `src/lib/server/rust-api.ts` (`API_INTERNAL_URL`).
- Uploads: `FormData` via proxy storage; do not set `Content-Type` manually.

## Structure

- `src/app/**/page.tsx`: thin `"use client"` re-exports.
- Real UI: `src/page-components/*.tsx` (+ feature components under `src/components/`).
- Auth modals: parallel route `@auth`.
- UI primitives: `src/components/ui/*` (Radix/shadcn). Match existing patterns; no new design system.

## i18n

Add every user-facing string to `src/i18n/translations.ts` for `pt|en|ja|es`. Use `useLanguage` / `TranslationWithParams`.

## Data fetching

Most pages use `useState`/`useEffect` + `lib/api`. Do not introduce React Query hooks unless the file already uses them (`QueryClient` only wraps the app).
